import Metronome.Strobes

/-!
# The elaborated chip-top operation strobes against `Metronome.Strobes`

Generated by `code/tests/lean/strobes_check.py` from the Yosys RTLIL of
`{{TOP}}` ({{KIND}}, case `{{CASE}}`).  Each definition below is the extracted
combinational cone of one strobe or selector of [project.v](../../../../src/project.v);
each theorem states that the extracted cone is the specification's function of
the move bus (and of the documented host decode), so the definition is the
specification on the elaborated cells.

What stays free is named in each theorem's arguments: `mv_en`, `grp_v`,
`c_dst`, `c_dat` (the core pipeline and the destination map are other cuts);
the picked word `w`/`mctl` (the group pick is `Metronome.Moves`), the host
decode `w_srt`, `a_srt`, `w_dbg`, `a_dbg`, `h_wd`, the queued configuration
write `cw_drain`, `cw_pending_addr`, and `cen`/`replay`.  Their provenance is
listed in `STROBES_NOTES.md`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option exponentiation.threshold 1024
set_option maxHeartbeats 8000000
set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

namespace Metronome.Strobes

open Metronome.CoreCtl (bitAt slice chain GroupWord makeWord)
open Metronome.Moves (atMostOne bits6 hitAt hitsMask pickWord hitOr symMask)

-- Generated from Yosys RTLIL. SHA-256 of the RTL snapshot: {{FINGERPRINT}}

{{BODY}}

{{AUDIT}}

end Metronome.Strobes
